  "caveats": [
    "The flux reference is arbitrary: the raw saves no magnetizing current, so only the swing and the period-to-period drift are measured.  cumulative_net_t is the drift accumulated from the start of this 120 us window, not the converter's absolute flux offset; cumulative_abs_t is the worst excursion if every period's imbalance had the same sign.",
    "The winding voltage includes L_leak*i (L_leak = 2.22 nH at k = 0.999); with the largest measured pair RMS the bound is 0.48 mT, which is leakage flux, not core flux.",
    "The deck's transformer is linear (no B-H curve, no core loss), so this is applied volt-seconds, not evidence about a saturating core.",
    "T2/T3 do not save their secondary voltages; the deck gives all four cores identical constants, so they are represented by T1/T4, not measured.",
    "The raw is the frozen 1 ms deck (4 mF output bank); the physical build uses 7.05 mF, which does not change the volt-second integral."
